The legal text is the Constitution of the Kingdom of Morocco, promulgated by Dahir n° 1-11-91 of
29 July 2011, in the French version published by the Ministère de la Justice du Royaume du Maroc on
its Adala portal (https://adala.justice.gov.ma/). The portal states no licence; the text is an
official legislative text, reproduced here unchanged apart from layout.

The Code pénal (dahir n° 1-59-413 du 28 joumada II 1382 (26 novembre 1962), consolidated to loi n° 33-18) is copied from the
text republished by WIPO Lex (https://wipolex-res.wipo.int/edocs/lexdocs/laws/fr/ma/ma088fr.pdf), retrieved 30 October 2026; credit
to WIPO Lex as the host. The PDF states no licence. Moroccan loi n° 2-00 relative aux droits d'auteur et droits voisins (dahir
n° 1-00-20 du 15 février 2000), article 8, provides: "La protection prévue par la présente loi ne s'étend pas : a) aux textes
officiels de nature législative, administrative ou judiciaire, ni à leurs traductions officielles". The code is therefore an
unprotected official legislative text.

The codes and texts added on 27 November 2026 are copied from two secondary hosts, named in each commit's
Source-status trailer and each folder's README.md:
- WIPO Lex (https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/): the Ministry of Justice's consolidated Code des obligations et des
  contrats, Code de commerce and Code de procédure civile, the Code du travail and other published texts; credit to
  WIPO Lex as the host. WIPO Lex states no licence on the PDFs.
- FAOLEX, the legislative database of the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations
  (https://faolex.fao.org/): Bulletin officiel texts (French edition). FAO's terms of use
  (https://www.fao.org/contact-us/terms/en/) allow FAO material to be copied and reused for non-commercial purposes
  with acknowledgement of FAO as the source; credit to FAO / FAOLEX as the host.
All of them are official legislative texts, which loi n° 2-00, article 8(a), quoted above, excludes from copyright.

The arrangement of this repository, its tables, commit messages and tools are by Lexifina and are dedicated to the
public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). This repository is not legal advice and not an
official publication.
